*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* All actions return via call to writepkt (op.writepkt):
*    bytes
*    0 - 1   server error status (see below)
*    2 - 5   status()
*    6+      action specific data
* Note op.writepkt adds the total packet length to the beginning of the packet sent,
*      and read_packet() in sdclilib.c 1st reads into structure:
*      struct {
*      int32_t packet_length;
*      int16_t server_error ALIGN2;
*      int32_t status ALIGN2;
*      } in_packet_header; 
*      Thus setting up the total data the c api (sdclilib.c) is expecting and status (server.error, status())
*
*
* All numbers in the client packets are low byte first regardless of the
* server platform byte ordering.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

* Server error status values
$define SV$OK               0    ;* Action successful
$define SV$ON.ERROR         1    ;* Action took ON ERROR clause
$define SV$ELSE             2    ;* Action took ELSE clause
$define SV$ERROR            3    ;* Action failed. Error text available
$define SV$LOCKED           4    ;* Took locked clause

$define MAX.ARG.COUNT     255

$define APILOGGING 0    ;* 0 = no log, 1 = log, >1 extra logging (full packet)

$internal
